# t1-doctor-image: the producers of js-runtime.json's nodeVersion (the doctor's script-runtime version)

Contract: native/core/crates/pending-wire/nr-exthost-doctor-updater.wire (Manifest.node_version, JsRuntime.node_version).
The doctor never spawns the interpreter, so the version must be written by whoever lays the install out. All paths are
under apps/desktop/scripts. Apply together with the core wire (the daemon's manifest reader denies unknown fields:
emitting nodeVersion before the reader accepts it breaks the daemon's start).

## core-layout.mjs

remoteJsRuntimeManifest(platform, arch) becomes remoteJsRuntimeManifest(platform, arch, nodeVersion) and its object gains,
after `electron: false,`:

    nodeVersion,

(a dotted version string of the pinned Node artifact, no leading "v"; throw when it does not match /^\d+\.\d+\.\d+$/).

verifyCoreInstall: for kind === 'remote' the expected manifest is built with the manifest's own nodeVersion
(`remoteJsRuntimeManifest(platform, arch, manifest.nodeVersion)`), so isDeepStrictEqual still pins every other field
and the version must be present and well formed; for kind === 'desktop' and for devJsRuntimeManifest nothing changes.

## stage-js-bundle.mjs (the line `await writeFile(join(payloadDir, JS_RUNTIME_MANIFEST), ...remoteJsRuntimeManifest(platform, arch)...`)

Pass the pin the file already holds: `remoteJsRuntimeManifest(platform, arch, node.version)`. (node.version is the version
of the Node artifact copied to js/node, the one sha256-checked above it.)

## core-layout.test.mjs / stage-js-bundle.test.mjs / core-layout-fixture.mjs

The remote fixtures and expected manifests carry the same nodeVersion; a remote manifest without it, or with "v22.20.0",
fails verifyCoreInstall.

## NOT produced here (open, needs an owner/lead decision; nothing is guessed)

- Desktop (desktopJsRuntimeManifest, stage-core.mjs): the interpreter is the Electron app in node mode. Its Node version is
  not known when resources are staged (the app is not built; the host Node's version is a different fact and must not be
  written). The only trusted source is the running app (process.versions.node, apps/desktop/src/main/index.ts, the value the
  desktop-start log already records). Handing it to mixdogd needs a launch channel (an argument or the existing handshake)
  in hot files (host/index.ts, connection.ts) and the daemon's compose; until one is chosen the desktop's doctor row reads
  Warn "Node.js script runtime version unavailable" instead of Ok.
- Dev installs (dev-core-install.mjs, devJsRuntimeManifest): the interpreter is whatever path the developer names; its
  version is not known without running it. Left unknown (same Warn).
